{"name":"Mom’s Love","hex":"#ffd4bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mangue."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Mother.\n\n used as a term of address for one's wife","used as a term of address for one's wife"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mom"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"},{"title":"Mother","blocks":[{"text":"A mother, mom, mum, mommy, or mummy is the female parent of a child. A woman may be considered a mother by virtue of having given birth, by raising a child who may or may not be her biological offspring, or by supplying her ovum for fertilisation in the case of gestational surrogacy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Portrait_of_a_woman_holding_a_baby_%28I0024828%29.jpg/330px-Portrait_of_a_woman_holding_a_baby_%28I0024828%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mother","wikidata":"Q7560"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa